# Fiscal agent release — do not repeat packaging failures

## Hard gate (before `./scripts/push-to-main.sh` or any tag)

When `apps/fiscal-agent/` **Go code** changed (especially `*_windows.go`):

```bash
./scripts/check-fiscal-agent.sh
```

This is **not optional**. It runs `go test` + `go vet` + **`GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build`** for Agent **and** Client.

Darwin `go test ./...` alone is **insufficient**: Windows build-tagged files are not compiled on macOS, so unused imports / syntax errors in `*_windows.go` only appear in the Windows cross-build (or CI). That already caused a broken main push + failed tag (`unsafe` unused in `fiscal_shell_windows.go` → 0.4.69 needed a second fix commit).

## Order that works

1. Code + `VERSION` + `RELEASE_NOTES.md` `## X.Y.Z`
2. **`./scripts/check-fiscal-agent.sh` must pass**
3. `./scripts/push-to-main.sh` (tag after push)
4. Wait for **fiscal-agent-release** green; confirm Release has `FarvooFiscalAgent-Setup-amd64.exe`
5. Only then tell the user the build is downloadable

## Forbidden

- Push/tag after only `go test` on Darwin
- Claiming downloadable from main merge without tag + Release assets
- Local macOS Setup/zip as a substitute for GitHub Release
- Editing `fiscal-agent-release.yml` unless changing the installer pipeline

See `docs/ci-and-release.zh.md` §踩坑.
